-Ufd1 AAA-ATPase complex is involved in degradation.", "slot_type": "causality", "source_span": "In addition to a role for the Cdc48-Npl4-Ufd1 AAA-ATPase complex , Doa1 and a mitochondrial pool of the transmembrane Cdc48 adaptor , Ubx2 , are implicated in their degradation ."}, {"fact": "Doa1 and Ubx2 are involved in degradation.", "slot_type": "causality", "source_span": "In addition to a role for the Cdc48-Npl4-Ufd1 AAA-ATPase complex , Doa1 and a mitochondrial pool of the transmembrane Cdc48 adaptor , Ubx2 , are implicated in their degradation ."}]}, {"article_id": "laysumm_elife_0070", "source_dataset": "eLife", "original_index": 70, "mode": "factuality_chase", "evidence_row_id": "row_0008", "abstract_sentence_idx": 8, "abstract_claim": "This study reveals a unique QC pathway comprised of a combination of cytosolic and mitochondrial factors that distinguish it from other cellular QC pathways.", "core_keep_af": "This study reveals a unique quality control (QC) pathway that combines cytosolic and mitochondrial factors.", "expert_summary_hint": "This showed that there were many similarities with how this process happen in other parts of the cell but that the precise combination of chaperones and enzymes involved was distinct.", "lay_context": "This research identifies a unique quality control pathway that involves a combination of factors from both the cell's cytosol and the mitochondria, distinguishing it from other cellular quality control mechanisms.", "story_role": "implication", "support_af_ids": ["laysumm_elife_0070_cand_0010", "laysumm_elife_0070_cand_0029", "laysumm_elife_0070_cand_0086"], "allowed_evidence_spans": ["This study reveals a unique QC pathway comprised of a combination of cytosolic and mitochondrial factors that distinguish it from other cellular QC pathways .", "Our results reveal a requirement for factors not previously implicated in the degradation of native MAD substrates and the combination of components identified defines a distinct QC pathway.", "These new mitochondrial model substrates have revealed a tightly-coupled degradation pathway at the MOM that requires both cytosolic and mitochondrial machinery."], "must_use_terms": ["unique QC pathway", "cytosolic factors", "mitochondrial factors", "distinguish"], "forbidden_overgeneralizations": ["the only QC pathway", "completely different"], "high_risk_check_facts": []}], "evidence_row_count": 8, "parse_error": false, "validation_errors": [], "raw_response": null}
