{"article_id": "laysumm_elife_0163", "source_dataset": "eLife", "original_index": 163, "mode": "factuality_chase", "model_key": "gemini25_flash_non_thinking", "evidence_rows": [{"article_id": "laysumm_elife_0163", "source_dataset": "eLife", "original_index": 163, "mode": "factuality_chase", "evidence_row_id": "row_0001", "abstract_sentence_idx": 1, "abstract_claim": "MicroRNAs (miRNAs) are conserved noncoding RNAs that function as posttranscriptional regulators of gene expression. miR-9 is one of the most abundant miRNAs in the brain.", "core_keep_af": "MicroRNAs (miRNAs) are conserved noncoding RNAs that regulate gene expression after transcription, and miR-9 is one of the most abundant microRNAs in the brain.", "expert_summary_hint": "A group of small RNA molecules called microRNAs have roles in controlling the development of neurons. One microRNA, called miR-9, is abundant in the brain.", "lay_context": "MicroRNAs are a type of RNA that help control how genes are expressed, and miR-9 is particularly common in the brain.", "story_role": "background", "support_af_ids": ["laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0001", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0002"], "allowed_evidence_spans": ["MicroRNAs ( miRNAs ) are conserved noncoding RNAs that function as posttranscriptional regulators of gene expression .", "miR-9 is one of the most abundant miRNAs in the brain ."], "must_use_terms": ["MicroRNAs", "miRNAs", "noncoding RNAs", "posttranscriptional regulators", "gene expression", "miR-9", "abundant", "brain"], "forbidden_overgeneralizations": ["miRNAs are the only regulators of gene expression", "miR-9 is the most abundant miRNA in the body"], "high_risk_check_facts": []}, {"article_id": "laysumm_elife_0163", "source_dataset": "eLife", "original_index": 163, "mode": "factuality_chase", "evidence_row_id": "row_0002", "abstract_sentence_idx": 2, "abstract_claim": "Although the function of miR-9 has been well characterized in neural progenitors, its role in dendritic and synaptic development remains largely unknown.", "core_keep_af": "While miR-9's function in neural progenitors is known, its role in dendritic and synaptic development was largely unknown.", "expert_summary_hint": "However, its role in the formation of dendrites and synapses remains unclear.", "lay_context": "Previous research had explored miR-9's role in early neuron development, but its involvement in the later stages of forming dendrites (tree-like structures on neurons) and synapses (connections between neurons) was not well understood.", "story_role": "motivation", "support_af_ids": ["laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0003", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0113"], "allowed_evidence_spans": ["Although the function of miR-9 has been well characterized in neural progenitors , its role in dendritic and synaptic development remains largely unknown .", "The function of miR-9 has been mainly studied in the context of neurogenesis , where it plays a role as a regulator of the balance between progenitor proliferation and neuronal differentiation ( Leucht et al . , 2008; Zhao et al . , 2009; Delaloy et al . , 2010; Bonev et al . , 2011; Coolen et al . , 2012 ) ."], "must_use_terms": ["miR-9", "neural progenitors", "dendritic development", "synaptic development", "unknown"], "forbidden_overgeneralizations": ["miR-9 has no known function", "all functions of miR-9 are unknown"], "high_risk_check_facts": []}, {"article_id": "laysumm_elife_0163", "source_dataset": "eLife", "original_index": 163, "mode": "factuality_chase", "evidence_row_id": "row_0003", "abstract_sentence_idx": 3, "abstract_claim": "In order to target miR-9 in vivo, we developed a transgenic miRNA sponge mouse line allowing conditional inactivation of the miR-9 family in a spatio-temporal-controlled manner.", "core_keep_af": "To study miR-9 in living organisms, researchers developed a transgenic miRNA sponge mouse line that allows for conditional and spatio-temporally controlled inactivation of the miR-9 family.", "expert_summary_hint": "A length of DNA, coding for an RNA molecule that binds to miR-9 molecules and stops them performing their normal function, was inserted into the mice.", "lay_context": "This new mouse model allowed the researchers to specifically turn off the miR-9 family in certain parts of the body and at specific times, which is crucial for understanding its precise roles.", "story_role": "method", "support_af_ids": ["laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0004", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0137", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0013"], "allowed_evidence_spans": ["In order to target miR-9 in vivo , we developed a transgenic miRNA sponge mouse line allowing conditional inactivation of the miR-9 family in a spatio-temporal-controlled manner .", "In summary , we describe the first transgenic sponge mouse line that allows for conditional inactivation of an miRNA family in a spatio-temporal-controlled manner .", "In order to efficiently knock-down miR-9 in a living animal , we employed miRNA sponges as a long-lasting miRNA inhibition strategy ."], "must_use_terms": ["transgenic miRNA sponge mouse line", "conditional inactivation", "miR-9 family", "spatio-temporal-controlled manner", "in vivo"], "forbidden_overgeneralizations": ["this is the only way to study miR-9", "this method inactivates all miRNAs"], "high_risk_check_facts": [{"fact": "The study describes the first conditional transgenic miRNA sponge mouse line.", "slot_type": "comparison", "source_span": "Here , we provide a new layer of complexity to the existing battery of in vivo tools for genetic manipulation of microRNAs by describing the first conditional transgenic miRNA sponge mouse line ."}]}, {"article_id": "laysumm_elife_0163", "source_dataset": "eLife", "original_index": 163, "mode": "factuality_chase", "evidence_row_id": "row_0004", "abstract_sentence_idx": 4, "abstract_claim": "Using this novel approach, we found that miR-9 controls dendritic growth and synaptic transmission in vivo.", "core_keep_af": "Using this new approach, the study found that miR-9 controls dendritic growth and synaptic transmission in living organisms.", "expert_summary_hint": "These experiments showed that miR-9 is involved in controlling dendrite growth and synaptic function.", "lay_context": "The experiments in the transgenic mice revealed that miR-9 plays a crucial role in the development of dendrites and the proper functioning of synapses.", "story_role": "finding", "support_af_ids": ["laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0005", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0019", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0058", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0059"], "allowed_evidence_spans": ["Using this novel approach , we found that miR-9 controls dendritic growth and synaptic transmission in vivo .", "Using the latter , we revealed a novel developmental role of miR-9 in the postmitotic differentiation of neurons , as a key regulator of dendritic growth and synaptic transmission in vivo .", "Figure 4 . miR-9 sponge transgenic mice exhibit dendritic growth defects and impaired synaptic transmission .", "Figure 4 . miR-9 sponge transgenic mice exhibit dendritic growth defects and impaired synaptic transmission ."], "must_use_terms": ["miR-9", "controls", "dendritic growth", "synaptic transmission", "in vivo"], "forbidden_overgeneralizations": ["miR-9 is the only factor controlling dendritic growth", "miR-9 directly causes all synaptic transmission"], "high_risk_check_facts": [{"fact": "Pyramidal CA1 neurons from miR-9-SpNestin-Cre mice showed reduced total dendritic length and arborization complexity compared to control littermates.", "slot_type": "comparison", "source_span": "Pyramidal CA1 neurons from miR-9-SpNestin-Cre mice exhibited a reduction in total dendritic length and arborization complexity compared to control littermates ( miR-9-Spfl-Stop ) ( Figure 4A–C ) ."}]}, {"article_id": "laysumm_elife_0163", "source_dataset": "eLife", "original_index": 163, "mode": "factuality_chase", "evidence_row_id": "row_0005", "abstract_sentence_idx": 5, "abstract_claim": "Furthermore, we demonstrate that miR-9-mediated downregulation of the transcriptional repressor REST is essential for proper dendritic growth.", "core_keep_af": "The study further demonstrated that miR-9-mediated downregulation of the transcriptional repressor REST is essential for proper dendritic growth.", "expert_summary_hint": "To enable a neuron to produce dendrites, miR-9 binds to and interferes with the RNA molecules that are needed to make a protein called REST. This protein is a transcription factor that switches off the expression of other genes so, in effect, miR-9 allows a set of genes that are needed for dendrite growth to be switched on.", "lay_context": "This means that miR-9 helps ensure dendrites grow correctly by reducing the activity of a protein called REST, which normally stops certain genes from being expressed.", "story_role": "mechanism", "support_af_ids": ["laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0006", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0020", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0099", "laysumm_elife_0163_cand_0090"], "allowed_evidence_spans": ["Furthermore , we demonstrate that miR-9-mediated downregulation of the transcriptional repressor REST is essential for proper dendritic growth .", "Furthermore , we show that regulation of the transcriptional repressor REST by miR-9 is essential for normal dendritic maturation .", "Importantly , we described an essential function of miR-9 in dendritic growth as a regulator of the expression of the transcriptional repressor REST .", "We observed that shREST transfection strongly rescued the dendritic growth defects in miR-9-SpNestin-Cre neurons ( Figure 5H ) , indicating that increased REST level is indeed the major mediator of miR-9 effects"], "must_use_terms": ["miR-9-mediated downregulation", "transcriptional repressor REST", "essential", "proper dendritic growth"], "forbidden_overgeneralizations": ["miR-9 is the only regulator of REST", "REST is the only factor affecting dendritic growth"], "high_risk_check_facts": [{"fact": "REST is a bona fide target of miR-9.", "slot_type": "causality", "source_span": "has been experimentally validated as a bona fide target of miR-9 ( Packer et al . , 2008 ) ."}]}], "evidence_row_count": 5, "parse_error": false, "validation_errors": [], "raw_response": null}
