ity_chase", "evidence_row_id": "row_0008", "abstract_sentence_idx": 14, "abstract_claim": "In short, we found a good correspondence between the Bayesian learning model and the empirical results indicating that this model poses a possible mechanism for simultaneously learning multiple visuomotor mappings.", "core_keep_af": "The good correspondence between the Bayesian learning model and empirical results suggests it provides a possible mechanism for simultaneously learning multiple visuomotor mappings.", "expert_summary_hint": "We developed a Bayesian learning model capturing these results . The model demonstrates that participants learn the set of separate shape-response pairs rather than their relationship .", "lay_context": "This model helps explain how the brain manages to learn and adapt to different motor responses based on various contextual cues.", "story_role": "implication", "support_af_ids": ["laysumm_plos_0228_cand_0016", "laysumm_plos_0228_cand_0017"], "allowed_evidence_spans": ["In short , we found a good correspondence between the Bayesian learning model and the empirical results indicating that this model poses a possible mechanism for simultaneously learning multiple visuomotor mappings ."], "must_use_terms": ["good correspondence", "Bayesian learning model", "empirical results", "possible mechanism", "simultaneously learning multiple visuomotor mappings"], "forbidden_overgeneralizations": ["only mechanism", "perfect match"], "high_risk_check_facts": []}], "evidence_row_count": 8, "parse_error": false, "validation_errors": [], "raw_response": null}
